==English==
{{wikipedia}}
{{wikipedia|Brisbane River}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|gd|bris||break, smash}} + {{inh|en|ang|bān||bone}}, a nickname given to someone who was often involved in fights, resulting in the breaking of bones. The city and river in Australia are named after {{w|Sir Thomas Brisbane}}, 1773–1860; governor of [[New South Wales]] (which at the time included the area of modern [[Queensland]]) from 1821 to 1825.

